    "result_text": "BUILD SUCCESS with the test passing. Let me summarize what I implemented.\n\n## Summary\n\nI redesigned owner identity so the `customerCode` is now `'<REGION>-<HASH8>'`, dropping the per-city sequence number, and moved every value derived from the customer code onto the new identity.\n\n### Changes\n\n**`OwnerRestControllerV1.java`** (`src/main/.../rest/controller/v1/`)\n- Replaced `nextCustomerCode(city, lastName)` (and its `prefix3` helper) with `customerCode(postcode, telephone, lastName)`, which builds `REGION-HASH8`:\n  - **REGION** = region code derived from the postcode (`NSW`/`VIC`/`QLD`, or `UNKNOWN`).\n  - **HASH8** = first 8 upper-case hex chars of `SHA-256(normalizedTelephone + lastName)`, via a new `sha256Hex8` helper. The telephone read here is the already-normalized E.164 value.\n- Updated the create call site to pass postcode/telephone/lastName.\n- Added `java.security.MessageDigest` / `NoSuchAlgorithmException` imports.\n- Repointed postcode validation to the renamed `LocalityDeriver.localityForCity`.\n\n**`LocalityDeriver.java`** (`src/main/.../mapper/`)\n- Added `region(postcode)` \u2014 postcode \u2192 region (the code embedded in the customer code).\n- Added `locality(customerCode)` \u2014 reads the `<REGION>` prefix back out of the customer code, so locality and the identity always agree.\n- Renamed the old city-table method to `localityForCity` (kept for postcode validation).\n\n**`OwnerMapper.java`** \u2014 `locality` now derives from `owner.getCustomerCode()` instead of city+postcode.\n\n**`openapi.yml`** \u2014 updated the `customerCode` and `locality` field docs to describe the new region-and-hash identity.\n\n### Automatically carried over (no code change needed)\n- **Membership number** (`<customerCode>-M<YY>`) and **check digit** (Luhn over the customer code's digits) both read `getCustomerCode()`, so they now reflect the new identity.\n- The **create audit record** logs `customerCode`, so it emits the new value (`AUDIT - owner created: ... customerCode=NSW-16E6609E ...`).\n\nThe test suite is green: `Tests run: 1, Failures: 0, Errors: 0` \u2014 `BUILD SUCCESS`.",
